<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 9.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 9.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Wednesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    355.56   2.24</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	    219.42   3.05</p>
<p> 3   Mayne Nickless	 181.90   8.24</p>
<p> 4   Colonial Coml	  124.04   2.27</p>
<p> 5   Adel Bton Cement     120.29   1.66</p>
<p> 6   Herald Rsc		90.27   1.02</p>
<p> 7   Forrestania Gold	83.87   2.34</p>
<p> 8   Countrywide-PP	  82.48   1.13</p>
<p> 9   Westral Forest	  79.71   2.20</p>
<p>10   Energy Equity	   74.10   1.03</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	     1.95   0.85</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    2.97   0.84</p>
<p> 3   Computer Power	   3.78   3.87</p>
<p> 4   Premier Inv		4.34   0.77</p>
<p> 5   Queensland Cotton	5.85   4.44</p>
<p> 6   Parbury Ltd		6.25   0.74</p>
<p> 7   BTR Plc		    6.56   6.10</p>
<p> 8   OLS Asia Hldgs	   7.06   0.84</p>
<p> 9   Aust Gold Rsc	    7.12   1.30</p>
<p>10   FAI Life ltd	     7.67   0.79</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
